course: dictionary
lesson: 8715
title: Sensibly means wisely
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sensibly is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something. Sensibly means in a wise, careful and practical way, so you think before you act. «Walk sensibly in the corridor» tells you how to walk: not running or pushing, but carefully and safely.
explain: Look at the words around it to find the meaning. «Be careful, washerwoman!» annoys him and he begins «to lose his head». To lose your head means to stop thinking clearly. So when someone acts sensibly, they are doing the opposite: they keep their head and think.
explain: Sensibly can also mean suitable for the situation. «Dress sensibly for the rain» means wear clothes that suit the weather, like a coat and boots. Try the swap test: put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Sensibly is an adverb, so it describes how an action is done.
fact: «Sensibly» means in a wise, sensible and practical way.
fact: «Sensibly» can also mean in a way that suits the situation, as in «dressed sensibly for the rain».
fact: To lose your head means to stop thinking sensibly.
fact: Other phrases with sensibly include «behave sensibly», «dress sensibly» and «sensibly priced».
exercise: «Please walk sensibly in the corridor.» What does sensibly mean here? | Pushing past everyone at top speed | *In a careful, safe way | Very loudly | With your eyes shut
exercise: Mum says, «Dress sensibly for the rain.» What should you wear? | *A warm coat and boots | A swimming costume | Shorts and sandals | A thin summer dress with no cover
exercise: Find the word that is closest in meaning to sensibly. | *Wisely | Noisily | Hurriedly | Angrily
test: «Use scissors sensibly.» What does this mean? | *Use them safely and carefully | Use them while running | Throw them across the room
test: «The shop sells sensibly priced bags.» What does sensibly priced suggest? | *Prices that are fair and reasonable | Prices written in another language | Very expensive prices
exam: Which choice shows someone acting sensibly? | He threw his bag into the pond | He lost his head and shouted at everyone | *She waited at the kerb and looked both ways before crossing | He ran across the road without looking
